# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DevJourney 365 — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in real values.
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser bundle.
# NEVER put the Supabase service-role key in this file or anywhere else in
# src/ — it would be shipped to every visitor. Service-role operations belong
# in server-side code only.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Project URL from Supabase → Project Settings → API.
# Format: https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# The public "anon" / "publishable" key. Safe to ship to the browser *provided*
# Row Level Security is enabled — which is what the migrations in supabase/
# are for. This is the key whose behaviour RLS governs.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional — AI integration (Phase 9, days 241–270)
#
# Leave blank to develop the rest of the app. When you reach the AI phase,
# create a key in Google AI Studio and set it here.
#
# NOTE: any VITE_* value is visible to users in the shipped bundle. Use this
# only with keys that are safe to expose, or proxy AI calls through a
# server-side function and keep the key out of the frontend.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=